WEBVTT

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:03.670
This looks bad.

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:06.290
They got all of the livestock,

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:09.300
and they destroyed a bunch of 
tools that can't be replaced.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.470
We'll have to go to Whitesails to buy more.

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:13.980
With what money?

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.660
Well, we won't be able 
to replace everything.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.590
Um... what is Whitesails?

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:23.060
Seriously, who <i>are</i> you?

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.810
Could you be any more sheltered?

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:26.130
Sorry.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:29.160
Uh, so... Whitesails is...

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:32.180
Oh, um... if you could tell me about 
the history of this place, too...

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:34.390
Yeah, fine.

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:38.590
You know this is the remote southern 
continent known as Southmark, right?

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:40.160
Yes, that I know.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:42.400
So around... two hundred years ago, was it?

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:45.940
Southmark was engulfed 
by a horde of demons.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:49.250
The Hundred Heroes took out 
the king of the demons,

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:51.500
but the humans abandoned this continent,

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:54.520
crossing the sea to retreat 
to Grassland in the north.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:58.240
<i>The Hundred Heroes... 
That's Blood and his buddies.</i>

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:02.160
Since the Fertile Kingdom unified the 
southwestern region of Grassland,

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:05.630
they've been cultivating the land with 
the intention of reclaiming it.

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:11.680
And Whitesails is the port town that became 
the center for immigration from the north.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:12.780
I see.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:16.120
A lot of folks with histories 
and aspiring heroes go there.

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:18.750
People who've received 
divine revelations, too.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:21.750
You're hoping to gather more faithful 
on this trip, too, right?

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:26.480
Gracefeel used to have a lot of devoted 
followers on the southern continent.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:27.930
Could you tell me more?

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:32.190
I think her followers were scattered 
in the Great Collapse...

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:33.540
Yeah, that's right.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:38.320
And the ones who managed to escape 
to Grassland kept her name alive.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:41.700
But still, her following 
has declined a lot.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:43.780
<i>Rampant demons and demon beasts,</i>

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:45.890
<i>villages that resort to thievery,</i>

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:47.890
<i>faith in the goddess dying out...</i>

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:52.450
Was doing something about all this 
the mission the goddess gave me?

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:55.830
Anyway, enough with the old legends.

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:57.680
We need to deal with the village first.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:00.070
Yeah, about that...

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:02.480
The people of this village have no money.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:05.040
Menel, wanna go explore some ruins?

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:06.520
We'll divide the loot evenly.

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:08.100
Huh?

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:19.160
The Faraway Paladin

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:42.980
I never would've guessed you'd 
be so good at scavenging ruins!

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:44.270
I'm used to them.

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:46.360
Seriously, who <i>are</i> you, anyway?

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:49.570
We did get enough money to 
rebuild because of it, though.

00:03:49.570 --> 00:03:51.660
We can even buy new livestock and tools.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:54.410
I made up for my own expenses, too.

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:56.200
I can't wait to get to town.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:58.630
When we do, the first thing 
we gotta do is eat.

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:00.420
The seafood in season right now is—

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:02.040
Someone!

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:03.560
Help!

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:07.750
A giant ape!

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:10.130
Hey! What are you doing?!

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:12.820
The two running from it are a 
halfling and... is that a hawker?

00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:13.280
Just throw that away already!

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:14.130
But—

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:15.930
No ifs, ands, or buts!

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:17.810
Oh, for crying out loud! Over here, you!

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:25.010
Come here!

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:25.540
Huh?

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:28.610
Who are you?

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:30.730
Wait, that's dangerous!

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:33.040
<i>Blood told me</i>

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:34.800
<i>that when facing a wild animal,</i>

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.280
<i>the moment you break eye contact, you lose.</i>

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:40.730
<i>Well, come at me if you're going to.</i>

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:42.500
<i>We can do a little wrestling.</i>

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:04.040
Thank goodness. I didn't have to fight it.

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:05.420
Are you okay?

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:08.070
Hey, who the heck are you?! An adventurer?!

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:11.710
Not many people can stop an agitated 
giant ape just by looking at it!

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:13.310
You're awesome! Awesome!

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:16.070
Oh! I'm Robina! Robina Goodfellow!

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:19.620
I'm a troubadour! I sing, I dance, 
I go where the wind takes me!

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:21.080
You can call me Bee!

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:23.840
And that dork over there 
is Antonio the hawker.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:25.360
I call him Tonio!

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:27.110
The company he worked for went under,

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:30.410
so now he passes himself off as a 
hawker on remote country roads!

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:34.620
I didn't even get a chance to speak.

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:38.090
I'm on my way back to 
Whitesails, my home base.

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:39.820
Whitesails?

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:41.970
Boy, you really saved our hides.

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:44.020
Thank you so much.

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:47.300
I'm Meneldor. I hunt around here.

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:49.930
We were just heading toward the 
town to do some shopping.

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:51.170
And that's...

00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:54.470
William. William G. Maryblood.

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:58.270
I'm a priest in service to Gracefeel, 
the goddess of light.

00:05:58.270 --> 00:05:59.620
You can call me Will.

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:01.830
Wow, that's a totally noble-sounding name!

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:04.690
And Gracefeel's the one they love 
in the southern continent, right?

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:07.890
Wow, wow! I didn't know 
she still had priests!

00:06:07.890 --> 00:06:09.890
And you're not just a priest, but a 
capable warrior priest! Aren't you?

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:11.370
Aren't you?! Aren't you?!

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:15.830
Yeah, he may look pretty spacey, 
but he's stupidly skilled.

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:19.260
I mean, I hardly ever get attacked by 
any beasts when I'm walking with him.

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:22.690
You mean the beasts know how 
strong he is and avoid him?!

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:24.190
What the heck?! That's so cool!

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:26.800
What? You usually see more?

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:28.230
Of course.

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:30.120
That's why this place 
is called Beast Woods.

00:06:30.940 --> 00:06:33.080
<i>It feels like their eyes 
are piercing me...</i>

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:35.280
Anyway, is it just the two of you?

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:37.000
No escort? Or were they killed?

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:41.210
Actually, when we ran into 
that giant ape back there...

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:43.510
I'm embarrassed to say that they ran away.

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:48.960
Some guys who were there for show conned 
you out of their up-front pay and bolted?

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:52.610
You gotta get some better 
judgment, peddler.

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:53.880
I'm so ashamed...

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:57.770
And they made a big ol' racket 
when they ran! It was nuts!

00:06:57.770 --> 00:07:01.400
Giant apes don't even attack people, 
usually. They just <i>look</i> scary!

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:04.100
<i>They both lost their guards?</i>

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:05.990
What are you going to do now?

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:08.930
We could take you with us, if you want.

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:10.820
We'll just say you owe us one.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:12.700
I'll do the deal-making, not you.

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:17.070
Owe you one... of what?

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:20.590
We want to buy some cows and 
horses and such in Whitesails.

00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:22.210
Ah, I get it.

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:25.000
If that's what you want, I'm glad to help.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:27.840
I'll introduce you to a dealer I know.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:31.170
We appreciate it. And sorry for butting in.

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:33.880
He doesn't know much about how 
the world works, you see.

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:36.750
Oh, so he really was born a noble?

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:40.590
He has that air about him! 
Like he's pure and untainted!

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:41.780
N-Nah...

00:07:41.780 --> 00:07:45.970
If I told you about my origins, 
I doubt you'd even believe me...

00:07:45.970 --> 00:07:49.740
You mean you're of such noble birth that 
you can't talk about your family?!

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:52.070
And a priest to an unsung god, no less!

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:54.010
Wow, that's fantastic! Fantastic!

00:07:54.010 --> 00:07:56.960
My bardic heart is filling 
with inspiration!

00:07:57.180 --> 00:07:58.910
R-Right...

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:02.750
<i>Wait... No matter what I say, 
it leads to misunderstandings...</i>

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:03.700
<i>What?</i>

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:06.230
Okay, that's settled. Let's get moving.

00:08:06.230 --> 00:08:08.560
Yeah! Let's go, let's go!

00:08:16.270 --> 00:08:18.640
Oh, this place looks perfect!

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:21.880
Whee! Here I am!

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:23.950
<i>Bee and Tonio warmed up to me quickly.</i>

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:28.020
<i>Tonio has a gentle demeanor, and he's 
good at getting close to others.</i>

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:32.100
<i>As for Bee, she doesn't seem to have 
any concept of distance from people.</i>

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:36.340
Okay, I guess it's time 
to give you all a song!

00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:39.650
Will, clap along for me, 
and collect any donations!

00:08:39.650 --> 00:08:41.790
Sure. You can count on me, Bee.

00:08:49.900 --> 00:08:57.320
<i>Listen now to these notes of gold...</i>

00:08:55.790 --> 00:08:57.190
It's amazing.

00:08:57.190 --> 00:09:00.120
Every time we walk into a village, 
she goes wild and gets everyone in on it.

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:03.160
She's always like that. 
I'm impressed she doesn't get tired.

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:04.260
I see.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:08.700
Then these items here should 
fulfill your needs.

00:09:05.450 --> 00:09:08.030
They make a good combination 
for doing business.

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:08.690
Huh?

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:13.480
A lot of hawkers use high-pressure 
tactics or even petty thievery.

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:11.600
She's hurt?

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:14.430
Let's see if I can get the
priest to take a look at it.

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:14.850
I see...

00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:17.680
Looks like he wasn't lying 
about working for a company.

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:18.680
Hey, Will...

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:21.500
there's something I'd like to ask you.

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:22.570
What is it?

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:28.070
Can the blessing you invoke 
heal sickness and injury?

00:09:28.070 --> 00:09:29.420
Yes, it can.

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:32.250
I see. Then I have a proposal for you.

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:35.420
Goddess of Light...

00:09:36.730 --> 00:09:38.620
You're all better now.

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:43.140
U-Um... How much do I owe you?

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:45.180
Oh, don't worry about that.

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:47.510
You can offer your gratitude to Gracefeel.

00:09:47.510 --> 00:09:51.430
And if Tonio has anything you like, 
please buy something from him.

00:09:51.430 --> 00:09:54.060
I'm still just in training.

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:57.370
Okay! Thank you so much!

00:09:57.740 --> 00:10:00.290
We'll get something to 
celebrate your recovery.

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:02.270
How about this hair ornament?

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:08.220
So Bee attracts people, Will offers 
healing, and both bring him business.

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:10.600
That Tonio's pretty smart.

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:14.130
Yeah. And it'll help with the return 
of the goddess of light, too.

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:16.600
That power of yours is pretty 
damn impressive, though.

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:21.310
Well, the blessing is a rewrite of 
reality through the power of a god.

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:24.560
That's how it can heal a wound 
as if it had never happened.

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:25.680
Huh...

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:28.640
I'm borrowing this power from the goddess.

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:32.000
I have to be careful not to 
mistake it for my own power.

00:10:32.710 --> 00:10:33.850
Wh-What?

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:36.360
Still in training, huh?

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:39.180
Er... I really am still training.

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:40.150
Will!

00:10:40.150 --> 00:10:41.600
Done with your free treatments?

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:42.720
Oh, yeah.

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:44.120
Then come with me!

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:44.770
Huh? What for?

00:10:44.770 --> 00:10:47.450
There's a party to celebrate 
everyone's recovery!

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:48.330
Right now?!

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:50.680
If they're at the party, 
she can sing again,

00:10:50.680 --> 00:10:52.980
and he can sell more goods.

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:54.870
He really is a good salesman.

00:10:57.950 --> 00:11:02.220
<i>We continued to pass through several 
villages, earning money in the same way,</i>

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:04.340
<i>as we made our way north 
for a couple of weeks.</i>

00:11:04.340 --> 00:11:06.000
<i>Then we emerged onto Wheat Road.</i>

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:11.170
Let's sleep over there tonight.

00:11:12.930 --> 00:11:16.080
Man, you guys went too 
crazy. It's already dark.

00:11:16.510 --> 00:11:17.660
Sorry about that.

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:20.200
I'm in a good mood today!

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:22.710
I'll give you a free performance!

00:11:22.710 --> 00:11:24.420
Wow, how generous of you.

00:11:24.420 --> 00:11:27.590
Hee hee! Now, what should I sing, I wonder?

00:11:27.590 --> 00:11:31.980
"Reystov the Penetrator" is 
too common these days...

00:11:33.050 --> 00:11:36.740
I know! How about the epic of the <i>Three Heroes</i> from <i>The Killing of the High King</i>,

00:11:36.740 --> 00:11:42.010
<i>The Wandering Sage</i>, <i>The War Ogre</i>, 
and <i>The Beloved Daughter of Mater</i>?

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:43.540
Ah, that sounds great.

00:11:43.540 --> 00:11:45.160
It's a fitting subject.

00:11:46.090 --> 00:11:48.870
I guess I haven't performed it for a while.

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:50.460
Hey, what's wrong, Will?

00:11:50.460 --> 00:11:52.500
Oh, it's nothing.

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:54.550
Go ahead and sing it. I'd love to hear it.

00:11:54.550 --> 00:11:57.740
Oh, I like that! You latched right on!

00:11:57.740 --> 00:11:59.750
Okay, let's get started!

00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:04.570
Time passes by... no, perhaps 
it is us who pass by.

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:09.100
Be it the strong warrior, the brilliant sage, 
or the holy woman,

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:13.910
with the turning of the moons, naught but 
their ashes and their names remain.

00:12:09.190 --> 00:12:11.760
<i>Their names really are remembered...</i>

00:12:14.190 --> 00:12:17.330
This is precisely why their 
song must be lifted up high,

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:19.310
with a prayer that their 
deeds live forever,

00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:22.590
that their heroic names resound 
throughout the world.

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:25.050
I sing this night of the Wyvern Killer,

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:28.740
one of the many heroic exploits 
of the Three Heroes.

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:30.980
Episode 8
Songs of Heroism

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:32.620
Keep quiet, now, and listen, all of you...

00:12:37.750 --> 00:12:43.120
<i>The demonblade forged by the stars...</i>

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:44.430
<i>Jeez, Blood...</i>

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:47.210
<i>You never talked about yourself at all.</i>

00:12:47.670 --> 00:12:49.580
<i>So this is what you did in your past.</i>

00:12:49.890 --> 00:12:54.880
<i>Casting aside any praise</i>

00:12:54.880 --> 00:13:00.560
<i>He kept his true name
concealed to the world</i>

00:13:00.560 --> 00:13:06.810
<i>Though time has passed,
his name is yet unknown</i>

00:13:02.870 --> 00:13:05.990
<i>So I guess no one knows 
Augustus's real name...</i>

00:13:06.810 --> 00:13:12.410
<i>She was as beautiful as a
princess from a faraway land</i>

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:19.620
<i>When asked about her lineage,
the healer would just gently smile</i>

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:20.800
<i>Mary's refined manner definitely gave 
the impression of noble origins,</i>

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:23.980
<i>but I'd believe it if someone told me 
she came from a poor village, too.</i>

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:30.170
These days are now long in the past.

00:13:30.170 --> 00:13:33.400
O countless wishes now 
left with no way home,

00:13:33.900 --> 00:13:38.830
I can but play your melody loudly, 
to be carried on the passing winds.

00:13:39.530 --> 00:13:42.750
<i>The story takes place before 
they were known as heroes,</i>

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:45.000
<i>when the three of them 
were traveling together.</i>

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:47.690
<i>A certain remote village that they visited</i>

00:13:47.690 --> 00:13:50.100
<i>was attacked by a wyvern,</i>

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:53.930
<i>and a beautiful half-elf was chosen 
as a sacrifice to appease it.</i>

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:58.070
<i>Upon hearing of this, 
Mary said they should save her,</i>

00:13:58.070 --> 00:14:00.930
<i>but Blood asked where they 
could possibly get the money,</i>

00:14:00.930 --> 00:14:02.750
<i>and Gus said nothing.</i>

00:14:03.350 --> 00:14:07.110
<i>Their personalities in the 
song are a bit off, I think.</i>

00:14:07.510 --> 00:14:12.960
<i>But still, it brings their voices, words, 
and expressions clearly to my mind.</i>

00:14:31.590 --> 00:14:32.940
Who are you?

00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:38.980
You think we're gonna take 
on a wyvern for that?

00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:48.990
Ah, what fine money. Look how it shines.

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:51.690
If we're given such fine payment...

00:14:51.690 --> 00:14:54.030
Then we have no choice but to do the job.

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:57.700
Damn, you're such pushovers. 
There's no profit in this.

00:14:57.700 --> 00:14:59.770
If it's not enough, I'll pay more!

00:14:59.770 --> 00:15:01.910
Sell me to a slave trader 
or whatever you want!

00:15:01.910 --> 00:15:03.790
You think even that would be enough?

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:10.930
But you do have some guts on ya.

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:13.260
You're small, but you're a warrior.

00:15:13.650 --> 00:15:18.710
It's only right to help a warrior who 
swallows his pride to ask for help.

00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:20.440
Let's do it.

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:21.500
Yes.

00:15:21.500 --> 00:15:22.350
Indeed.

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:31.780
Ligatur!

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:31.700
Be Tied

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:32.450
Nodus!

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:32.320
Knot

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:33.410
Binding

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:33.520
Obligatio!

00:16:09.290 --> 00:16:11.660
So what're you gonna do now?

00:16:11.660 --> 00:16:14.560
Neither of you can stay 
in that village anymore.

00:16:14.830 --> 00:16:16.190
We'll figure it out.

00:16:17.030 --> 00:16:18.700
Then take this with you.

00:16:18.700 --> 00:16:21.310
Old Gus here carved Words on it.

00:16:21.310 --> 00:16:23.780
It'll serve you better than 
some cheap good luck charm.

00:16:24.260 --> 00:16:28.250
You can't be a warrior if you don't 
have at least one dagger, after all.

00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:30.380
Take this, as well.

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:33.710
Take care of yourselves, and of each other.

00:16:33.710 --> 00:16:35.870
You will face many difficulties,

00:16:35.870 --> 00:16:38.320
but never forget the value of perseverance.

00:16:38.320 --> 00:16:40.440
This is more than what I paid you!

00:16:40.440 --> 00:16:41.980
We can't accept this.

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:44.490
Hah! Who said we were giving it to you?

00:16:44.490 --> 00:16:47.560
It's an investment. 
We're only lending it to you.

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:48.590
Lending?

00:16:48.590 --> 00:16:49.560
Listen.

00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:52.100
You two must live the best you can,

00:16:52.100 --> 00:16:54.590
build up savings, and make 
names for yourselves.

00:16:54.590 --> 00:16:57.030
If your names someday reach our ears,

00:16:57.030 --> 00:17:01.290
we will come to collect what 
we've lent you, plus interest.

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:05.440
In preparation, I will 
give you my real name.

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:08.730
This will be our password. Listen well.

00:17:08.730 --> 00:17:12.680
Thus the boy and girl learned the 
true name of the Wandering Sage,

00:17:12.680 --> 00:17:15.960
known to no one else in the world.

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:20.110
Hand in hand, the boy and girl 
made their way to the city,

00:17:20.110 --> 00:17:25.970
and the Three Heroes walked down the 
road in search of a new adventure.

00:17:26.430 --> 00:17:28.740
That's the end of the song,

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:30.890
but there's more to the story.

00:17:30.890 --> 00:17:33.150
Count Dagger of the Fertile Kingdom...

00:17:33.150 --> 00:17:36.440
His actual surname was Wizardsdagger.

00:17:36.680 --> 00:17:41.410
To this day, an elderly half-elf 
woman still waits at his mansion.

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:42.660
<i>Does that mean...</i>

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:47.750
She believes someone who knows the sage's 
true name will come to her one day,

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:50.230
so that she can return what he lent to her,

00:17:50.230 --> 00:17:52.740
along with what he lent to her husband.

00:17:53.080 --> 00:17:57.300
She plans to offer her thanks 
to him when that day comes.

00:17:57.300 --> 00:17:59.380
That's what the story is about...

00:17:59.380 --> 00:18:03.320
A story of three great heroes 
that still echoes to this day.

00:18:03.320 --> 00:18:06.180
Huh? Will, are you crying?

00:18:06.180 --> 00:18:09.080
N-No, I'm not. I'm not crying.

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:11.120
Aw, c'mon, now!

00:18:11.120 --> 00:18:15.000
You must've been really 
moved by Bee's story, huh?

00:18:14.410 --> 00:18:16.800
No, it's not that!

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:18.150
Aw, don't be shy!

00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:23.500
<i>There are still many people in this 
world who remember you three.</i>

00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:25.290
<i>There always were.</i>

00:18:25.940 --> 00:18:29.000
<i>That makes me so happy.</i>

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:39.010
<i>The Fertile Kingdom, huh?</i>

00:18:39.330 --> 00:18:43.360
<i>Once we cross the sea, we'll meet people who 
still talk about Blood and the others.</i>

00:18:44.880 --> 00:18:45.700
Hi there.

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:48.760
You're working hard.

00:18:48.760 --> 00:18:49.950
Tonio.

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:53.730
Will, you are strong.

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:55.070
You think so?

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:59.750
I can clearly see how polished 
your movements are.

00:18:59.750 --> 00:19:03.110
Then again, maybe you don't 
want to hear that from a guy

00:19:03.110 --> 00:19:05.710
who got conned by phony adventurers...

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:10.280
But you're obviously used to 
handling that fine dwarven spear.

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:14.340
Anyone who can wield a dwarven masterpiece 
is a masterpiece themselves.

00:19:14.660 --> 00:19:17.580
But there's one thing I don't understand.

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:20.210
Something you don't understand?

00:19:20.210 --> 00:19:23.030
What is it that you want?

00:19:23.030 --> 00:19:25.840
What do I... Why do you ask?

00:19:25.840 --> 00:19:28.250
Because I'm a merchant.

00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:33.410
It's my job to move merchandise 
and grant people's wishes

00:19:33.410 --> 00:19:36.610
in exchange for fair compensation.

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:38.790
You are quite a mystery.

00:19:39.130 --> 00:19:42.800
I've never met anyone like you before.

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:45.500
You are strong, and you have courage.

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:47.660
You have good manners, you are educated,

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:49.610
and you aren't hurting for money.

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:52.260
But you're not quite like a noble.

00:19:52.260 --> 00:19:55.960
You're more like a holy knight 
I've heard stories about.

00:19:57.750 --> 00:20:01.500
Which is why I decided to ask you directly.

00:20:01.910 --> 00:20:05.360
What is it that you, 
as an individual, wish for?

00:20:05.360 --> 00:20:09.900
Or are you strictly a representative 
for your goddess?

00:20:10.300 --> 00:20:12.330
Um... I...

00:20:12.860 --> 00:20:16.220
I had a happy little life up until now,

00:20:16.220 --> 00:20:19.050
but I lost it shortly before 
I set out on my own.

00:20:19.640 --> 00:20:22.950
I gained the divine protection of 
the goddess of light in its place.

00:20:24.130 --> 00:20:27.410
I still don't know anything 
about this world.

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:30.250
So I want to start by learning about it.

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:32.690
I think that, among the things I learn,

00:20:32.690 --> 00:20:35.490
I'll find what it is I want.

00:20:35.930 --> 00:20:40.670
Oh... and friends. 
I also want companions, I guess.

00:20:40.900 --> 00:20:43.310
Is Menel not your friend?

00:20:43.310 --> 00:20:44.880
Well, actually...

00:20:44.880 --> 00:20:47.410
I think we get along fairly well,

00:20:47.410 --> 00:20:50.510
but he won't acknowledge me as a friend.

00:20:50.900 --> 00:20:55.240
He just calls me "priest," 
like he's putting me on a pedestal.

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:58.830
Yeah... I want friends.

00:20:59.450 --> 00:21:00.750
I see.

00:21:00.750 --> 00:21:04.520
Then perhaps I'll volunteer for 
the third-place position.

00:21:04.520 --> 00:21:05.230
Huh?

00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:09.960
Menel and Robina would be angry 
if I tried to get ahead of them.

00:21:09.960 --> 00:21:11.640
That would be scary.

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:17.870
Well, shall we get some water 
and start preparing breakfast?

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:18.940
Okay.

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:22.710
Here you go.

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:24.810
It's so good!

00:21:24.810 --> 00:21:27.930
It really is. You're a great cook, Tonio.

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:29.250
He sure is!

00:21:29.250 --> 00:21:32.630
To tell you the truth, 
that's why I travel with him!

00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:37.130
We're eating a lot better 
now, thanks to Tonio.

00:21:37.130 --> 00:21:39.620
Yeah, since you can't cook worth a lick.

00:21:39.620 --> 00:21:40.920
Well, I...

00:21:41.510 --> 00:21:44.190
Your cooking isn't so hot either, Menel!

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:46.070
What? All you gotta do is eat it.

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:50.200
And we always get bread 
from Will at lunchtime.

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:53.550
Isn't that so cool? 
He prays, and bread appears!

00:21:53.550 --> 00:21:56.170
I'd prefer to stop as little as possible,

00:21:56.170 --> 00:21:59.050
so I'm grateful to have 
food I can eat as I walk.

00:21:59.050 --> 00:22:02.230
Then let's get ready to leave 
as soon as we're done eating.

00:22:02.230 --> 00:22:02.890
Yeah.

00:22:03.410 --> 00:22:05.930
You ask when we will return home,

00:22:05.930 --> 00:22:08.290
but there is no way to know 
when we will return.

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:10.870
By the way, what's going 
on at Whitesails now?

00:22:08.290 --> 00:22:10.850
As the rain falls, the water 
in the lake stagnates,

00:22:10.850 --> 00:22:12.160
and the two fall silent.

00:22:10.870 --> 00:22:13.480
I've been holing up in 
Beast Woods for a while,

00:22:12.160 --> 00:22:16.630
As the rain pounds, someday, 
someday... ah, someday...

00:22:13.480 --> 00:22:15.390
so I haven't been to the port in ages.

00:22:15.390 --> 00:22:18.480
A new ruler has taken over 
the Fertile Kingdom.

00:22:16.630 --> 00:22:19.380
the two will draw closer together.

00:22:18.480 --> 00:22:19.890
So Egbert II is...

00:22:19.890 --> 00:22:21.980
His posthumous name is "Egbert the Bold."

00:22:21.980 --> 00:22:24.360
He wasn't a half-bad king.

00:22:24.360 --> 00:22:27.100
I see... So he's dead...

00:22:27.100 --> 00:22:29.310
Yes... but there's a bit of a problem.

00:22:29.700 --> 00:22:32.720
His legitimate heir, 
Prince Owen, succeeded him,

00:22:32.720 --> 00:22:34.420
but he falls short of his father,

00:22:34.420 --> 00:22:38.460
and the lords have suggested that 
now is the time to advance south.

00:22:38.660 --> 00:22:40.450
That sounds bad...

00:22:40.450 --> 00:22:44.700
Fortunately, this hasn't had any 
great effect on Southmark yet.

00:22:44.700 --> 00:22:49.720
The king's brother, who was dispatched 
to Whitesails, is a great, wise man.

00:22:49.720 --> 00:22:53.320
The crown prince, Ethelbald Rex Fertile.

00:22:53.320 --> 00:22:55.910
He comes from a different 
mother than King Owen,

00:22:55.910 --> 00:22:58.950
but he excels with both the pen 
and the sword, like his father.

00:22:59.380 --> 00:23:02.190
It is due to Prince Ethel's rule

00:23:02.190 --> 00:23:04.840
that the government of 
Whitesails continues to run.

00:23:05.360 --> 00:23:07.720
Sounds like a complicated situation...

00:23:11.020 --> 00:23:11.650
Will!

00:23:12.090 --> 00:23:13.840
C'mon, this way!

00:23:12.700 --> 00:23:13.620
What now?

00:23:14.160 --> 00:23:16.150
This is your first time seeing it, right?

00:23:16.410 --> 00:23:17.420
There, look!

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:21.500
<i>The city...</i>

00:23:22.610 --> 00:23:28.580
<i>Just one symbol of what Blood, Mary, 
and Gus gave their lives to protect.</i>

00:23:29.760 --> 00:23:32.640
That's Whitesails!

00:23:35.510 --> 00:23:39.970
Episode 9
Whitesails
